WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.330
It is tempting to rank
countries by one number:

2
00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.410
income per person.

3
00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:10.660
In 1990, the United Nations Development
Programme began publishing something different:

4
00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:12.620
a single score for a country,

5
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.340
from 0 to 1.

6
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.880
Yet two countries with
the same income can land

7
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.530
far apart on it.

8
00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:21.810
So if two countries earn
the same income per person,

9
00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.390
how can one be far more developed?

10
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.490
In this mission, you'll pull
that score apart and see

11
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:28.790
what goes into it.

12
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.440
Then you'll test other measures,

13
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.410
and find what even the
best of them leave out.

14
00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:36.620
Your mission: find out how
two countries with the same

15
00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.970
income per person can be
so differently developed.
